uot;post_date&quot;:&quot;2023-12-25T17:22:01.506Z&quot;,&quot;cover_image&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mAiV!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F860c3fa9-2165-4d52-9eae-9f9d7933401d.heic&quot;,&quot;cover_image_alt&quot;:null,&quot;canonical_url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/mushrooms-the-original-christmas&quot;,&quot;section_name&quot;:&quot;RAMHT&quot;,&quot;video_upload_id&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:139980281,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;newsletter&quot;,&quot;reaction_count&quot;:14,&quot;comment_count&quot;:0,&quot;publication_id&quot;:355550,&quot;publication_name&quot;:&quot;The Frontier Psychiatrists &quot;,&quot;publication_logo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!oO3w!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F997b8496-9b4d-43c2-b393-6f8a77945b00_1080x1080.png&quot;,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;youtube_url&quot;:null,&quot;show_links&quot;:null,&quot;feed_url&quot;:null}\"></div><div class=\"digest-post-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;nodeId&quot;:&quot;90877525-028c-4a9f-9de8-3a0db8de75c3&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;I'm lucky to have the friends that I have. One of those is Grady Hannah, who gave me a nudge several years back.&quot;,&quot;cta&quot;:null,&quot;showBylines&quot;:true,&quot;showDescription&quot;:true,&quot;showImage&quot;:true,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;md&quot;,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Join Us at RAMHT-AI This Sunday in San Fransisco.&quot;,&quot;publishedBylines&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:2277375,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Owen Scott Muir, M.D.&quot;,&quot;bio&quot;:&quot;Dr. Owen Scott Muir, M.D., DFAACAP is the Chief Medical Officer of Radial &amp; Neurolief. He's a graduate of Amherst College, Child, Adolescent, and Adult Psychiatrist, and a prolific writer and podcaster. https://www.meetradial.com for more.&quot;,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1c03f44d-4506-4843-989f-0d38e66c6946_400x400.jpeg&quot;,&quot;is_guest&quot;:false,&quot;bestseller_tier&quot;:100}],&quot;post_date&quot;:&quot;2026-01-09T14:00:53.233Z&quot;,&quot;cover_image&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!aQm4!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F35b5a60c-ca71-428d-9bf1-ca313528ecb7_4027x1088.jpeg&quot;,&quot;cover_image_alt&quot;:null,&quot;canonical_url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/join-us-at-ramht-ai-this-sunday-in&quot;,&quot;section_name&quot;:null,&quot;video_upload_id&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:184016819,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;newsletter&quot;,&quot;reaction_count&quot;:6,&quot;comment_count&quot;:1,&quot;publication_id&quot;:355550,&quot;publication_name&quot;:&quot;The Frontier Psychiatrists &quot;,&quot;publication_logo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!oO3w!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F997b8496-9b4d-43c2-b393-6f8a77945b00_1080x1080.png&quot;,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;youtube_url&quot;:null,&quot;show_links&quot;:null,&quot;feed_url&quot;:null}\"></div><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/ramht-psych-congress-september-14th?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/ramht-psych-congress-september-14th?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p>","text":"I have some very exciting news to share: RAMHT is expanding our event calendar and will be bringing the show to New Orleans on September 14 th !\n\nOur theme — Building the Practice of Tomorrow, Today — reflects our ongoing efforts to transform the future of brain medicine, accelerate access to innovative mental health treatments, and foster a community of experts and advocates dedicated to improving lives.\n\nOk, this is Rush at MSG, not RAMHT, but it’s pretty close.\n\nLed by me, Dr. Owen Muir , and my team mate in life, Dr. Carlene MacMillan , of this very The Frontier Psychiatrists Substack – along with Grady Hannah , Co-Founder of NightWare and RAMHT – the event aims to connect audiences with the leaders shaping the future of psychiatry through:\n\n• Rapid-fire 1:1 talks daring to ask the big questions and address the elephants in the room.\n\n• Conversations focused on where interventional psychiatry is heading and how scientific discovery is being translated into real-world impact.\n\nIf you’re a nurse practitioner, psychiatrist, psychologist, researcher, resident or advocate, stop sitting through the usual, dry panels!\n\nJoin us for an engaging evening of discussions focused on breakthroughs in mental health care that are guaranteed to be both entertaining and impactful.\n\nSpeakers who’ll help us explore a range of advancements in rapid acting mental health treatments include:\n\n• Jessica Malberg, PhD , Executive Director, Medical Affairs, Definium Therapeutics\n\n• Colleen Hanlon, PhD , VP of Global Medical Affairs, BrainsWay\n\n• Andrew Penn, RN, NP, CNS, PMHNP-BC , Director of Clinical Nursing Operations, Salma Health\n\n• Kate Passanisi, MBA , Managing Director, CareNetGPO\n\n• Tobias Marton, MD, PhD , Chief Medical Officer, Mindful Health Solutions\n\n• Steve Beller , Chief Commercial Officer, Neurorelief\n\n• Kazu Okuda MD , Founder & CEO, Universal Brain\n\n• Jay Pathmanathan MD, PhD , Medical Director, Beacon Biosignals\n\n• Prantik Kundu, PhD , Co-Founder & CEO, EyeThree\n\nAnd many thanks to our sponsors Definium Therapeutics , BrainsWay , Universal Brain , Radial , Salma Health , Neurolief , mdhub . Not only are they working tirelessly to transform the future of brain medicine, but they are instrumental partners in making RAMHT possible as a live forum.\n\nSo, block your calendar for September 14 th and grab your FREE ticket via Eventbrite!\n\nWe’ll be sharing more details on speakers, rapid-fire talks and panel discussions on the RAMHT website and LinkedIn page (follow us if you’re not!).\n\nStay tuned, get excited for more & see you in New Orleans! Also, we will have special guests. And surprises. And maybe….just maybe… embarrassing merch, for me, personally.\n\nGet your FREE RAMHT Tickets\n\nPrior RAMHT-themed content includes:\n\nShare"}